A||N||10||beachbomb||Clutch pedal/Idle comments||||12||
Z||000000||beachbomb||12-27-2000||04:24 PM||||Hey all, well i finally got around to changing out my broken clutch pedal, after a pulled neck and hurt back ITs COMPLETE!! talk about a bid difference, i no longer have to mash the pedal all the way to the floor to change gears, very smooth now, i never knew it would make this big of difference.<BR>second topic: my idle still hangs around 1500rpm, list of things i have changed/replaced: o2 sensor, tps, vss, tbi, iac, all temp sensors, tbi gasket, ignition coil, altenator, plug wires, plugs, distributor and rotor, replaced all vacuum hoses, no leaks, ecm, fuel filter,Whats left? it will still try to idle, goes to about 1000 then right back up to 1500 and stays there until next on/off cycle. I even did the "spray WD-40 on the intake manifold gasket to see if the idle rises", but it didn't, stayed at 1500. Is there anything i'm missing?..plmk, thanks..Jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||12
Z||000001||beachbomb||12-27-2000||04:27 PM||||Sorry, to add to the above, i also checked the timing. After doing all the above i can honestly say i have the smoothest running car in town!!!! , thanks..Jim||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||12-27-2000||04:59 PM||||LMAO, wow, bet those chiropractor bils are outrageous. <P>Sounds like it should run pretty smooth after all that. <P>I'm not a (car)mechanic by any means so I cna't offer any advice for your idle problem. Glad to hear that the pedal made the different on the clutch though. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||horseman||12-27-2000||06:27 PM||||Hey Jim,<BR>How difficult was it to replace the pedal?<BR>I think mine may be bent, and I find myself pushing it to the floor as well. Could you explain the process?<BR>Thanks,<BR>Charlie||||reg||5
Z||000004||JohnnyK||12-27-2000||06:33 PM||||I find myself pushing the pedal too the floor too. Course, I also find myself losing clutch fluid from somewhere!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||beachbomb||12-27-2000||07:33 PM||||Hey Jeff, no kidding, i didn't realize how small of a space that was until i tried to get in it!!!<BR>By the way, about another post, i plan on keeping the interior on my extra Indy, as a spare for my good Indy. Sorry! It would look good in your car though!<P>Horseman- its wasn't really all that hard, just really difficult working position! here is a link that explains the process, it works like a champ, its what i used:  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/arch6.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/arch6.htm</A>  <P>mine had a broken pedal(the flat thingy your foot pushes on, it basically broke into a million pieces!) all i had left was the arm coming down, i don't know if it was bent or not, just know it works alot better now than before, lmk how your changeout goes! Good luck!..Jim(2 '84 Indys) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||chrissherman||12-28-2000||02:51 AM||||Try binding the stop on the TBI just a little.The little arm pointing at the drivers seat now you wont have to drill out the idile stop screw plug it worked on my 84 4cyl 4speed||||reg||1
Z||000007||chrissherman||12-28-2000||02:53 AM||||Try binding the stop on the TBI just a little.The little arm pointing at the drivers seat now you wont have to drill out the idile stop screw plug it worked on my 84 4cyl 4speed||||reg||1
Z||000008||chrissherman||12-28-2000||03:05 AM||||try binding the idile stop on the TBI just a little so you dont have to pop the plug on the idile stop screw It worked on my 84 4cyl 4speed||||reg||1
Z||000009||chrissherman||12-28-2000||03:06 AM||||try binding the idile stop on the TBI just a little so you dont have to pop the plug on the idile stop screw It worked on my 84 4cyl 4speed||||reg||1
Z||000010||chrissherman||12-28-2000||03:22 AM||||Try binding the idile stop arm just a little so you dont have to pop the idile screw plug cap it worked on my 84 4cyl 4speed||||reg||3
